# Tailwind And Component Practices

When creating or updating UI components in this project:

- Prefer Tailwind utility classes for layout, spacing, typography, and responsive behavior.
- Use `cn()` from `src/cn.ts` when classes are conditional, breakpoint-heavy, or composed from multiple variants.
- Keep plain static class strings without `cn()` when no conditional logic is needed.
- Use local `<style>` CSS only when utilities are not enough (pseudo-elements, browser-specific selectors, or complex cases).
- Keep CSS minimal and colocated in the same component when needed.
- Extract repeated UI patterns into reusable Astro components instead of duplicating markup.
- Keep component props clear and typed; use sensible defaults for content variants.
- Reuse existing icons, design tokens, and shared components before creating new ones.
- Prioritize readability: small focused components, consistent naming, and shallow nesting.
